{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgdXsAS9VNwZL3W8DR3vJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When the author of a link blog tested Moonshot's new Kimi K3.1 Pro, the command saved two separate outputs: the model's answer and its reasoning trace. The model, released on the Kimi API on October 23, supports three reasoning effort levels, low, medium and max, and the author ran the same prompt, an SVG of a pelican riding a bicycle, at each one. The test used the \"llm openai endpoint\" command, which works with any OpenAI-compatible endpoint but does not log results, so the author redirected standard output to one file and the reasoning trace, written to standard error, to another.\n\nFor anyone evaluating the model, the reasoning levels add a variable to cost and latency on top of the price list. Moonshot charges $2.00 per million input tokens and $10 per million output tokens, the same as GPT-6.1 Sol and half the price of Claude Opus 5.5, and its \"Highspeed\" version runs 2 to 3 times faster at twice the price, except for input cache hits, which cost the same. The article does not report how token usage or speed changed across the three reasoning levels, so the pelican runs show what each setting produced without measuring what each one costs.\n\nOn capability, Artificial Analysis scored K3.1 Pro at 55, behind only Claude Opus 5.5 at 58 and ahead of Claude Fable 5.1, GPT-6 Astra and Gemini 4 Argon at 53. Moonshot's own benchmarks claim the model is roughly level with Opus 5.5 and GPT-6 Astra. The model is API-only for now, with Moonshot promising \"Full model weights will be released by Nov 4, 2026.\" The blog's author called it the first time a soon-to-be open-weight model has scored this highly against the frontier, a distinction that will hold once those weights are actually published."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":925,"cache_read_input_tokens":6141,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":925},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7941065a-4d6b-4fc5-9521-ad25f07eb469","uuid":"e5fea4c8-644d-47f1-b818-da6fd77922b9","timestamp":"2026-11-02T05:16:12.432Z","request_id":"req_011CgdXs9z7YhmyCuXuQfbcX"}
